      "latin": "cōticula, cōticulae f.",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "modern",
      "gloss": "a pencil sharpener",
      "evidence": [
        "M-O s.v. pen: pencil-sharpener"
      ],
      "comment": "The diminutive of <span lang=\"la\">cōs</span>, a whetstone: classically a small touchstone for testing gold (Plin. NH 33.126) or a small stone mortar (Plin. NH 31.100, Lewis &amp; Short). To sharpen a pencil is <span lang=\"la\">graphium acuere</span>, as one sharpens a blade (<span lang=\"la\">ferrum acuere</span>, Verg. A. 8.386, Lewis &amp; Short)."
    },
    {
      "latin": "īnstrūmentum cuspidārium",
      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "modern",
      "gloss": "a pencil sharpener",
      "evidence": [
        "Traupman 358"
      ],
      "comment": "A tool for points (<span lang=\"la\">cuspis</span>, a point); the adjective <span lang=\"la\">cuspidārius</span> is not in Lewis &amp; Short."
    },
    {
      "latin": "cuspidārium, cuspidāriī n.",
      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "modern",
      "evidence": [
        "Andresian p. 12"
      ],
      "comment": "Traupman’s adjective made a noun: the thing that gives a point (<span lang=\"la\">cuspis</span>)."
    }
  ],
  "phrases": [
    {
      "latin": "Graphium acuendum est; cedo cōticulam.",
      "english": "The pencil needs sharpening; pass me the sharpener.",
